    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d252">

                <pb facs="0430" n="328" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg328"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 General Committee/701</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-09">December 9, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador left with me this morning the accompanying <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>. He asked whether we had received from
                    Berlin the Chancellor’s proposal referred to in the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >mémoire</hi>. I told him that we had not received anything recently on the
                    subject. Sir Ronald said that he would telegraph London that he had delivered
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">mémoire</hi> and, at the same time, he would inform
                    his Government that we had not received a copy of the German proposal. The
                    Ambassador asked that his communication be kept strictly confidential.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d252-a1.xml" xpointer="d252-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
